      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Traveling on the Eurostar is a bit like a high-speed train ride, but you have to be careful with your luggage because the rules are stricter than a typical train. You can bring up to 70kg of checked baggage, but there's a catch: if you have more than one piece of checked luggage, each piece must weigh no more than 23kg. If you have only one piece of checked luggage, it can weigh up to 125kg, but it must be at least 23kg. If you have more than one piece of checked luggage, each piece must weigh no more than 23kg. If you have only one piece of checked luggage, it can weigh up to 125kg, but it must be at least 23kg. Wait, that's a bit confusing. Let me rephrase. You can bring up to 70kg of checked baggage, but if you have more than one piece, each piece must be no more than 23kg. If you have only one piece, it can be up to 125kg. Hand luggage is limited to 40cm x 25cm x 23cm.",
